{"id":"NCT04494074","title":"Fever Control Using External Cooling in Mechanically Ventilated Patients With Septic Shock","official":"Intérêt du Traitement de la fièvre Par Refroidissement Externe Pour la Survie Des Patients ventilés en Choc Septique","summary":"The best strategy for managing fever in patients with septic shock remains unknown. In a pilot study, the investigators showed that fever control at normothermia allowed a better control of shock and evolution of organ failures. In this second trial the investigators will conduct a multicentre, open-label, randomized controlled, superiority trial in which two strategies will be compared:\n\n1. Respect of fever\n2. Fever control at normothermia using external cooling The primary end point will be d-60 mortality.","conditions":["Septic Shock"],"interventions":[{"type":"OTHER","name":"External Cooling"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Documented or suspected infection either communautary or hospital acquired\n* Septic shock defined by the need for vasopressor and lactate\\>2 mmol/l despite adequate fluid resuscitation (sepsis-3 definition)\n* Patients under invasive mechanical ventilation\n* Body core temperature\\>38.3°C\n* Intravenous sedation or opioids\n* Ongoing antimicrobial treatment and/or intervention for infection source control\n* Attending physician confirms clinical equipoise without substantial risk if the patient participates in the trial\n* Informed consent of next of kin/other designated person before inclusion or procedure for inclusion in emergency situation\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* Cardiac arrest within previous 7 days\n* Acute brain injury within previous 7 days\n* Extensive burns or epidermal necrolysis\n* \\<18 years old\n* Body core temperature \\>41°C\n* Under legal guardianship\n* No affiliation with the French health-care system\n* Pregnancy\n* Participation in another interventional study with mortality as the primary endpoint\n* An investigator's decision not to resuscitate\n* Patient already recruited in the trial","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":820,"start":"2022-10-01","pcd":"2028-12-01","upd":"2026-09-21","sponsor":"Centre Hospitalier Intercommunal Creteil","areas":["other"],"central":["Frédérique SCHORTGEN, MD · 01 57 02 34 11 · Frederique.schortgen@chicreteil.fr","Camille JUNG, MD · 01 57 02 22 68 · camille.jung@chicreteil.fr"],"sites":[{"f":"CHU Amiens","city":"Amiens","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":49.9,"lon":2.3,"c":"Julien MAIZEL, MD · Maizel.Julien@chu-amiens.fr"},{"f":"CHU Angers","city":"Angers","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":47.4716,"lon":-0.552,"c":"ASFAR Pierre, MD · PiAsfar@chu-angers.fr"},{"f":"CH Victor Dupouy","city":"Argenteuil","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":48.9479,"lon":2.2474,"c":"Gaetan PLANTEFEVE, MD · gaetan.plantefeve@ch-argenteuil.fr"},{"f":"Hôpital Nord Franche Comté","city":"Belfort","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":47.6422,"lon":6.8539,"c":"Julio BADIE, MD · Julio.BADIE@hnfc.fr"},{"f":"CH Cholet","city":"Cholet","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":47.0589,"lon":-0.8797,"c":"Julien DUPEYRAT, MD · julien.dupeyrat@ch-cholet.fr"},{"f":"Centre hospitalier intercommunal de Créteil","city":"Créteil","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":48.7927,"lon":2.4657,"c":"SCHORTGEN Frédérique, MD · Frederique.schortgen@chicreteil.fr"},{"f":"Hôpital Henri Mondor","city":"Créteil","pr":"","zip":"","s":"ANR","lat":48.7927,"lon":2.4657,"c":""},{"f":"CHD Dijon","city":"Dijon","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":47.3134,"lon":5.0139,"c":"QUENOT Jean Pierre, MD · jean-pierre.quenot@chu-dijon.fr"},{"f":"CHU Grenoble","city":"Grenoble","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":45.1787,"lon":5.7148,"c":"Guillaume DUMAS, MD · GDumasgalant@chu-grenoble.fr"},{"f":"GH Est Francilien","city":"Jossigny","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":48.8376,"lon":2.7543,"c":"Ly Van Phach VONG, MD · lvpvong@ghef.fr"},{"f":"CHD Vendée","city":"La Roche-sur-Yon","pr":"","zip":"","s":"R","lat":